n\nThe reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-875bc03a-5e72-5af8-9376-22adf38e16a5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-875bc03a-5e72-5af8-9376-22adf38e16a5" :answer-field/id #uuid "875bc03a-5e72-5af8-9376-22adf38e16a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-65028e55-3a8b-521e-8771-7d7fd0667387" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a818e102-2e5b-547e-9d5e-908647988fcb" "answer-d6825204-482f-5521-8bda-c88be8485051" "answer-65028e55-3a8b-521e-8771-7d7fd0667387" "answer-aa1f3aad-6a31-57d1-aef1-e79d1174936a" "answer-66b70f53-aa24-525d-8ce3-88738f313f32"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a818e102-2e5b-547e-9d5e-908647988fcb" :answer/id #uuid "a818e102-2e5b-547e-9d5e-908647988fcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6825204-482f-5521-8bda-c88be8485051" :answer/id #uuid "d6825204-482f-5521-8bda-c88be8485051" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65028e55-3a8b-521e-8771-7d7fd0667387" :answer/id #uuid "65028e55-3a8b-521e-8771-7d7fd0667387" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa1f3aad-6a31-57d1-aef1-e79d1174936a" :answer/id #uuid "aa1f3aad-6a31-57d1-aef1-e79d1174936a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66b70f53-aa24-525d-8ce3-88738f313f32" :answer/id #uuid "66b70f53-aa24-525d-8ce3-88738f313f32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a35aea07-c94b-5a19-9d28-82b8ec3131d0" :question/id #uuid "a35aea07-c94b-5a19-9d28-82b8ec3131d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-139966" :question/problem "If \n$W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 4 & -7\\end{aligned}]$, then $\\text{rank}(W)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the rank of $H,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 4 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(W)=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-53d401b7-f4a5-53bf-90cd-e38c287d2cd7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-53d401b7-f4a5-53bf-90cd-e38c287d2cd7" :answer-field/id #uuid "53d401b7-f4a5-53bf-90cd-e38c287d2cd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3f6df2aa-3a3c-5b79-95be-3aa1251322e5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b3662759-0a3a-5444-ae02-4e604c768bf6" "answer-50ede2f9-25a2-5752-be09-6a03468fd702" "answer-d0c17d6f-b6f3-5934-a787-839b47f6354b" "answer-3f6df2aa-3a3c-5b79-95be-3aa1251322e5" "answer-14c4ed15-45f5-58b1-8360-553b48f39d3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3662759-0a3a-5444-ae02-4e604c768bf6" :answer/id #uuid "b3662759-0a3a-5444-ae02-4e604c768bf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-50ede2f9-25a2-5752-be09-6a03468fd702" :answer/id #uuid "50ede2f9-25a2-5752-be09-6a03468fd702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0c17d6f-b6f3-5934-a787-839b47f6354b" :answer/id #uuid "d0c17d6f-b6f3-5934-a787-839b47f6354b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f6df2aa-3a3c-5b79-95be-3aa1251322e5" :answer/id #uuid "3f6df2aa-3a3c-5b79-95be-3aa1251322e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14c4ed15-45f5-58b1-8360-553b48f39d3a" :answer/id #uuid "14c4ed15-45f5-58b1-8360-553b48f39d3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-06e82198-39dc-5c74-b637-e63de9108225" :question/id #uuid "06e82198-39dc-5c74-b637-e63de9108225" :question/math-academy-id "q-34763" :question/problem "If $D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{rank}(D)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the rank of $D,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(D)=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-70236281-7f70-52d0-841b-4b25aab4bef3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-70236281-7f70-52d0-841b-4b25aab4bef3" :answer-field/id #uuid "70236281-7f70-52d0-841b-4b25aab4bef3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0b20e34e-3de9-55a2-9483-aacb5be32d8f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4508060c-7fe7-5a16-bd3e-18d84d0901d9" "answer-7d77b117-d7d3-56fe-b224-a19869996959" "answer-70622a79-c9d6-529b-9225-ebaa52284a66" "answer-0b20e34e-3de9-55a2-9483-aacb5be32d8f" "answer-17628bca-0c14-5472-acd0-2fe108d7530a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4508060c-7fe7-5a16-bd3e-18d84d0901d9" :answer/id #uuid "4508060c-7fe7-5a16-bd3e-18d84d0901d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d77b117-d7d3-56fe-b224-a19869996959" :answer/id #uuid "7d77b117-d7d3-56fe-b224-a19869996959" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70622a79-c9d6-529b-9225-ebaa52284a66" :answer/id #uuid "70622a79-c9d6-529b-9225-ebaa52284a66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b20e34e-3de9-55a2-9483-aacb5be32d8f" :answer/id #uuid "0b20e34e-3de9-55a2-9483-aacb5be32d8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17628bca-0c14-5472-acd0-2fe108d7530a" :answer/id #uuid "17628bca-0c14-5472-acd0-2fe108d7530a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121058 :tutorial/content "The dimension of the column space of a matrix $A$ is called the **rank of $A$**. It's usually denoted by $\\textrm{rank}(A)$. So, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A) = \\textrm{dim}(\\textrm{Col}(A)).\n$$\n\nFor example, to find the rank of \n![](images/b9/b91bd53b8f1807be516e2477b37fbcd9c3a7415d6cf848d84aa085bc510b5eb4.svg)\nwe write $A$ in row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that there are $2$ pivot columns, namely, the $1$st and the $2$nd. This implies that the first and the second columns of $A$ form a basis of $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ and, therefore, the dimension of $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is equal to $2.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121068 :tutorial/content "Note that the number of pivot columns always coincides with the number of non-zero rows in the corresponding row echelon form matrix.\nSo, technically, \n\n$\\textrm{rank}(A)$ is the number of *pivot columns* in the corresponding row echelon form matrix of $A$.\n\nOr, equivalently,\n\n$\\textrm{rank}(A)$ is the number of *non-zero rows* in the corresponding row echelon form matrix of $A$." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120057 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
